  "doc": "Ansedra's crowd (act2_ch13 A02, the zone note and barks 1-2; the Lead, 2026-10-30: Act II crowds from the bodies that exist). Barge-polers in plain grey at the outer moorings (the stand-in `ansedra` community), Tenders in Order robes, pilgrims from the islands standing at the causeways' edges, a child who doesn't play. Clear of the walkways and the story marks (kerrid_moorings, sefir_door, house_sefir, corran_house, pact_sefir). No birds, no dogs, no games (rule 4). Each row's `at` makes its stand-in at CrowdSpots/<id> (VillagerLayer). Stillguard at the bridges and the named people are the characters track's. The vignettes on the outer moorings (the Lead, 2026-10-30: the Act II towns lived in; ground probed 2026-10-30), clear of the causeway's mouth: the polers' families: a girl and her brother at a clapping game, a girl at stones, a woman with a basket come down to the barges, a woman folding the barge's grey awning at the rail, a poler mending a net, an old poler sweeping the top edge.",
